---
import '@fontsource-variable/roboto-serif';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '28 August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="How intentionaut.com handles your data: the newsletter, the contact form, and analytics. Plain English."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>What happens to your data here.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is a small site with a newsletter and a contact form. Here is
        everything it collects, who processes it, and how to get it removed. In
        plain English. It is not legal advice, and I keep it current as the site
        changes.
      </p>
      <p class="article-meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        Intentionaut Ltd (Saielle DaSilva) is the data controller for this site.
        Reach me at <a href="mailto:hello@intentionaut.com">hello@intentionaut.com</a>
        for anything on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        When you subscribe, I collect your email address. The newsletter runs on
        <a href="https://www.beehiiv.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">beehiiv</a>,
        which stores your address, records whether you open or click issues, and
        logs your IP address and approximate location at the moment you sign up.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is your consent: you tick the consent box, and a
        confirmation email checks it was really you. You can withdraw consent at
        any time using the unsubscribe link in every issue, or by emailing me.
        Unsubscribing removes you from future sends; beehiiv may keep a
        suppression record so you are not accidentally re-added.
      </p>
      <p>
        beehiiv is based in the United States. That transfer is covered by
        beehiiv's data processing terms and standard contractual clauses.
      </p>

      <h2>The contact form</h2>
      <p>
        If you write in, I collect your name, email address and message. The
        message is delivered to my inbox through
        <a href="https://www.mailgun.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mailgun</a>
        (EU region). A
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/products/turnstile/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Turnstile</a>
        check runs on the form to keep bots out; it processes limited technical
        and device signals and does not track you across sites.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is my legitimate interest in replying to you and, where
        relevant, taking steps towards working together. I keep the message as
        long as it is relevant to your enquiry or an engagement, then delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        The site uses
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>,
        which counts page views in aggregate. It sets no cookies, uses no
        cross-site identifier, and is not used to identify anyone. That is why
        there is no cookie banner: there is nothing personal to consent to.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served through GitHub Pages and Cloudflare (CDN and DNS).
        Their standard server logs apply while a page is being delivered to you.
      </p>

      <h2>What I never do</h2>
      <p>
        No selling your data. No advertising trackers. No sharing beyond the
        processors named above, which only act on my instructions.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK GDPR you can ask me to give you a copy of your data, correct it,
        delete it, restrict or object to its use, or hand it to another service.
        You can withdraw consent for the newsletter at any time. Email
        <a href="mailto:hello@intentionaut.com">hello@intentionaut.com</a> and I
        will act on it. If you are not happy with how I have handled something,
        you can complain to the
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>This site is not aimed at anyone under 16.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the new version and its date go here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .article-meta {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .prose {
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }
</style>
